@startuml cca-overview
set separator ::

!include ./CCA-Nucleus.def.iuml
!include ./CCA-Contracts.def.iuml

class Registry {
	registerCapability(CapabilityDescriptor)
	bindCapabilities(consumer, provider, contractType)
	CapabilityDescriptor[] getInitializationOrder()
}

note as noteRegistry
	The Capability Registry is 
	the central coordination point that:
	* Manages all capabilities and their metadata
	* Tracks contracts and bindings
	* Actively prevents circular dependencies!
	* Provides topological sorting for initialization order
	* Enables dependency injection
end note

class CapabilityDescriptor {
	+createInstance(): CapabilityInstance
}

class CapabilityInstance {
	-essence
	-realizationImpl[]
	-dependencies[]
	+void initialize()
	+void start()
	+void stop()
	+void releaseResources()
	+void closeConnections()
	+void cleanup()
}

class CapabilityLifecycleManager {
	-registry
	-initializedCapabilities[]
	+void initializeAll()
	-void initializeCapability(CapabilityDescriptor)
	+void shutdownAll()
	-void shutdownCapability(CapabilityInstance)
}
CapabilityLifecycleManager o--> Registry
CapabilityLifecycleManager ..> CapabilityDescriptor
CapabilityLifecycleManager ..> CapabilityInstance : use

CapabilityDescriptor ..> CapabilityInstance : creates

hide members

@enduml
